WEBVTT

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.520
Once upon a time, lands were plentiful.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.480
People were content.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:16.050
However, a greedy man took all the fruit, seed, and livestock as his own.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.680
People cried in hunger.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.770
Upon hearing their cries, a brave warrior appeared.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:29.810
With her spear clad in blue flames, she pierced the heart of the greedy man.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.630
The lands became plentiful once more.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.920
The greedy man was named Darksen.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.730
The brave warrior was named Valkyria.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.960
Chapter 1:

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.960
War Encounter

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.930
Stay calm and move orderly!

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.230
The Gallian Army will protect you when

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.700
you get to the town of Landbaste!

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.120
Be well. I'm sure you'll be able to return here soon enough.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.300
Ragnite and ragnoline will be distributed at Landbaste.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.680
Please don't throw away your ration coupons.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.900
Hans!

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.180
Alicia!

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.380
Thank goodness, Alicia.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.560
You'll be in trouble if you get lost here.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.180
She's right, Hans.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.490
The scary Imperial Army will catch you and eat you!

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:41.250
Don't worry, Alicia and the town watch will take care of them!

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.490
Right?

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:48.720
Of course! The Bruhl town watch won't lose to the Imperial Army!

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.710
Yes!

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.390
But the commander of the Imperial Army is strong, isn't he?

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:57.470
I heard the Ghirlandaio Fort fell in three days.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.340
He's the Crown Prince Maximilian, if I remember correctly.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.420
I'm sure he's a commander that's just for show!

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.160
He must be weak.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.900
I sure hope so...

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.810
Hey!

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.510
This is the last bread I baked at my house this morning.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.910
Thanks, Ma'am.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.110
I'm sorry I wasn't able to help you.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:27.040
What are you saying? Your work at the town watch is more important.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:33.300
Besides, you've always been helping out at our shop ever since my husband passed away.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.240
The bread you bake is already Meister-level.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.610
Please be safe.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.820
You too.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.050
If there's anything, just contact me.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:47.900
Come.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:10.960
Alicia!

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:18.280
What's wrong, Susie? What about your work?

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.720
A spy's here!

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.420
He's around the Dabos Bridge! He's alone!

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.720
He's a young man.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.380
Is that really so?

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.910
Jan and Miguro are keeping watch over him.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:37.070
But I don't think he's noticed us, yet.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.640
When will Mr. Laaken be back?

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.240
In the afternoon?

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.790
What do we do?

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:48.310
What if the spy is armed?

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.830
I'm scared.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.530
I shouldn't have joined the town watch.

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.740
Susie, guard this place for me.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.600
Alicia!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.760
Where's the spy?

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.190
Oh, so it's just you, Alicia.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.860
Over there. He's alone at the moment.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.150
He's writing something in his notebook.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.330
Notebook?

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.530
Look. He's definitely a spy.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.330
Don't move.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.290
Slowly put your hands over your head and turn around.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.450
We're from the Bruhl town watch.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.630
What are you doing here?

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.650
I'm making a sketch of the shining trout.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:51.750
Shining trout? Do you have any idea what kind of situation we're in?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.590
Huh? Did I do something wrong?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.330
Show me your notebook.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.980
What kind of code is this?

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.230
What? You don't know about the shining trout?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:08.120
Every spring it swims upstream.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.240
I sketched it to record the patterns on the trout's body.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.740
The shining trout around Bruhl have an especially fascinating pattern.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:16.710
Not only that, today's a nice, warm day!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.290
Right, right. I'll confiscate your notebook.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.010
You can't do that-

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.500
Don't move.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.760
We'll listen to what you have to say at the town watch's guardhouse.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:34.840
What a bother... I didn't know sketching was prohibited.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.440
Are all Imperial soldiers as carefree as you?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.260
Imperial soldiers?

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:44.150
I wonder... I don't know about them.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.930
I don't believe it... can he carry out a mission like that?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:54.370
Oh, I haven't asked your name.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.890
What's your name?

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.100
Welkin.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.530
Welkin Gunther...

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:03.210
Who was the one who thought up that name?

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.010
You don't look like you know, so let me tell you.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.220
You need certain qualities to call yourself a Gunther. The qualities of a hero.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.060
You're not fit to call yourself a Gunther, Mr. Spy.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.020
Huh, a spy? Me?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.850
Stop pretending!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.530
I really have no idea what you're talking about.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:22.230
Huh? When did I become a spy?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.610
Huh?! Spy?!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.690
It's too late to deny-

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.660
An emergency callback? What's going on?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.790
I'm going back first.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.800
Take him with you. Don't let him escape!

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.300
Just leave it to us!

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:49.210
What's going on? Do you know anything?

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.250
Be quiet!

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.150
Like we'd tell you anything!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:56.610
Do you also think I'm a spy?

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:00.950
Be careful, Miguro. This man is trying to talk us into releasing him.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.810
That's not my intention...

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:12.660
You boys look like you're barely fifteen, and you've already joined the town watch?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.530
Yes, so what? But don't look down on us!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:21.790
The Gallians have military drills since elementary school. We can even drive tanks!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.650
But that thing's so worn-out it can't move.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.340
It's fine, we don't have to tell the truth.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.570
But, but... we only sat in the gunner's seat.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.440
It'd be so uncool if he found out.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.220
Shut up, Miguro!

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.640
Welkin! Aren't you Welkin?

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:41.930
Martha!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:47.230
How are you feeling? It's almost time if I'm not wrong.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:50.150
Everything's going fine. Thanks for asking.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:54.130
Have you met Isara?

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.240
No, I was just about to.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.960
Hurry and go see her.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.950
She said she won't leave the house until you return.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:05.160
Isara's a stubborn one.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.830
She just cares a lot about her brother.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.410
Welkin, what's with your hands?

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.160
This is... Well...

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:18.580
Are you up to no good again?

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.560
Hey, you!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.230
Don't go off by yourself!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.400
It's nothing.

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.660
Take care of yourself, Mrs. Martha!

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:29.440
Welkin!

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:39.450
We confirmed the presence of the Imperial Army in the Bellib Forest.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.820
It won't take even half a day for them to reach here if they move quickly!

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.660
Yes, that's correct.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.060
Mr. Laaken, what's the military doing?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:57.320
It will take twenty four hours before the order to dispatch is issued.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:03.180
They're too slow! Why do they have to take so long?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.980
Taking the war situation into account, we're probably deemed to be lower priority.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.690
Are they telling us to wait for the town to be invaded?

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:14.080
If we make the first move, we may be able to drive the Imperials back!

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.120
Melkel, we should have the evacuation of the townspeople as our top priority.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.640
All right, about our deployment in the afternoon...

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:25.160
Who is it?

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:30.020
Umm... Alicia?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:34.110
Jan! We're having an important discussion right now! Come back later!

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.060
But...

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:38.300
Actually, at the Dabos Bridge-

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:42.260
Alicia, this isn't the time to be listening to children's nonsense.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.230
I'll be back in a moment.

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:52.020
It's this man! He was talking to a woman.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.580
He's definitely suspicious!

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.570
We know each other...

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:01.660
We're busy now. You'll have to wait here for the time being.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.930
May I ask you something?

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:06.990
Go ahead.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:10.630
Is a battle going to take place in Bruhl?

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:14.490
Are you their informant?!

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.300
I'm not!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.200
Then how do you know?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.100
The siren sounded and you came back here in a hurry.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:25.460
And many people in the town watch are gathered here.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.100
Which can only mean something bad has happened.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.230
To you, it's good news, isn't it?

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.330
Can you release me?

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.620
There's someone waiting for me.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.410
I'll be back as soon as I can. Will you let me go?

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.420
You're kidding me!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.370
Who would believe what you say?

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.230
Jan, Miguro, keep watch over him.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.050
Be very careful.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:54.960
Roger!

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:00.050
Are the Imperials really going to attack us?

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:03.680
What are you-

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.860
Both Jan and I are members of the town watch too!

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:09.890
We hate to be kept in the dark!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:22.120
The Imperials... The East European Imperial Alliance and the Atlantic Federation are at war over the mineral, Ragnite.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:28.910
Since Gallia is abundant in Ragnite, the Imperials set their sight on us and started a war.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:31.240
You learned all of this in class, right?

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:36.270
Gallia has to fight to protect herself.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.750
The town watch has to protect the townspeople.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.380
We intend to discuss the specifics afterwards.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.270
But I believe we might need to evacuate all the townspeople by today.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:11.860
Well then, the first to third shift will be in charge of traffic control and body-guarding.

00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.410
The fourth shift onward will patrol the town.

00:12:14.990 --> 00:12:18.260
I shall make another request for the military to dispatch here.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:22.580
It'll make a considerable difference if
they dispatch even a small troop here.

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:28.570
After that, we can only hope that the Imperial
Army will take their time in reaching this place.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.060
Hey, Alicia.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.310
We won't get shot, will we?

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:53.000
We just have to shoot before we're shot. It'll be all right!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:57.700
I-I can't do a thing like that! Aren't you afraid?

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.500
It's all for the sake of protecting Bruhl.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:14.770
He-

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.190
He's running away!

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.450
Hold it right there!

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:23.290
I'm sorry!

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.530
I'll shoot if you don't stop!

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.040
I'll really shoot!

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.620
It's pointless to try to escape.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.130
The Imperial Army!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.100
Scouts...

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.420
They've already reached this place.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.350
Who's waiting for you?

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.940
My younger sister.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:29.790
Younger sister?

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:33.360
Whose sister? Your sister?

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:34.010
Yes.

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:38.120
Impossible. You were sketching so leisurely just a while ago.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.850
If your sister's waiting for you, you should be hurrying back instead!

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:45.180
I'm often told that my priorities are strange.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:50.810
Honestly, I'm getting lost just by talking to you.

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.110
All right. But I'm going with you.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:58.100
That's the condition, okay?

00:14:58.860 --> 00:14:59.820
If you try anything funny-

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.560
Thank you! I'm very grateful!

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.580
Where's your house?

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.540
It's in this direction.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:11.170
Go this way and we'll reach it in about fifteen minutes.

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:12.800
Wait a second!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.280
The house over there is General Gunther's mansion-

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:19.710
Take cover!

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.950
Come out, Gallian soldiers!

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:25.320
Run!

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.370
Over here!

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:00.830
Let's enter the mansion from the inner door.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.470
Why do you know so much about this mansion?

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.140
This is the home of General Gunther!

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:11.580
He's the hero who saved Gallia in the First European War.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.640
So it seems.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:14.630
Don't tell me-

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.930
Everyone tells me that all the time.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.910
Really? Gunther's your-

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:21.070
Get down!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:25.690
Oh no, we're being chased.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:27.520
This way!

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:39.750
Wait!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.110
Isara!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.910
Welkin!

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:04.530
Welkin!

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:07.080
Thank God... you're all right.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.490
Let me introduce you. She's-

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.960
So you were lying after all.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.060
Lying?

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:17.370
You said you're the general's son, and you were going to fetch your sister.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.780
What do you mean, sister? She's a Darksen!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.830
It's not a lie! Isara's my-

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.240
Raise your hands!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:55.980
Isara...

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.300
We have weapons in the shed.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:15.990
It's an old model, but it should work.

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:17.800
What's that?

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.250
Grenades.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:21.330
They're relics from the First European war.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:22.950
They can still work!

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:28.220
A carefree elder brother and a reliable younger sister, huh?

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:31.650
Here, take this.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:34.950
Thanks.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:39.350
My name's Alicia. Alicia Melchiott.

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.620
I'm Isara.

00:18:41.230 --> 00:18:46.250
I swear that from now on, I won't sketch shining trouts before asking for permission.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.810
Fire!

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:07.460
I'll teach you what will happen to you...

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.630
... if you belittle the town watch, Imps!

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:17.850
I did it!

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:24.210
Oh, sorry. Excuse me!

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:26.650
You're really taking it easy, Welkin.

00:19:26.650 --> 00:19:29.820
I'll treat you to sandwiches if we get out of this safely.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.670
Made with Bruhl's most delicious bread!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.350
Are we ready?

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:40.710
Umm, there's one more thing I'd like you to use.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.400
It's a bit big, though.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.930
Isara, you don't mean...

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:46.630
What is it?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:49.680
This.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.280
This...

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:14.890
Greetings! I'm Alicia Melchiott.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:18.720
I work at the bakery, but I'm in the Bruhl town watch too.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:22.720
That's why I won't forgive the Imperial Army!

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:27.700
The biggest problem now is how to
escape from General Gunther's home.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.080
Can I <i>really</i> trust Welkin?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.630
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles, Chapter 2.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.110
<i>Prayers Falling Like Snow</i>.

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:41.040
Chapter Two:

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:41.040
Prayers Falling Like Snow

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:40.620
